{"abstract":"Active learning aims to select the minimum amount of data to train a model that performs similarly to a model trained with the entire dataset. We study the potential of active learning for image segmentation in underwater infrastructure inspection tasks, where large amounts of data are typically collected. The pipeline inspection images are usually semantically repetitive but with great variations in quality. We use mutual information as the acquisition function, calculated using Monte Carlo dropout. HyperSeg is trained using active learning with an underwater pipeline inspection dataset of over 50,000 images. To allow reproducibility and assess the framework’s effectiveness, the CamVid dataset was also utilized. For the pipeline dataset, HyperSeg with active learning achieved 67.5% meanIoU using 12.5% of the data, and 61.4 % with the same amount of randomly selected images. This shows that using active learning for segmentation models in underwater inspection tasks can lower the cost significantly.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ribeiro Marnet, Luiza","Grasshof, Stella","Brodskiy, Yuri","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730182"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Active learning","Computer vision","Underwater inspection"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["EIVA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"uncertainty driven active learning for image segmentation in underwater inspection","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2403.14002.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-730182","ids":["itu-950ebbcc-5a10-4ece-919f-f1beb600add2"],"keyword":["Active learning","Computer vision","Underwater inspection"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-15FA40FC63DF05822113463C38168637"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2403.14002.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.14002","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["EIVA"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luiza","key":"ribeiromarnetpau","last":"Ribeiro Marnet","name":"Ribeiro Marnet, Luiza","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"graßhofpau","last":"Graßhof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","name_org":"Graßhof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuri","key":"brodskiypau","last":"Brodskiy","name":"Brodskiy, Yuri","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"]},"sid":["itu-950ebbcc-5a10-4ece-919f-f1beb600add2"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Uncertainty Driven Active Learning for Image Segmentation in Underwater Inspection","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-730182","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Whereas the semantics of probabilistic languages has been extensively studied, specification languages for their properties have received less attention---with the notable exception of recent and on-going efforts by Joost-Pieter Katoen and collaborators. In this paper, we revisit probabilistic dynamic logic (pDL), a specification logic for programs in the probabilistic guarded command language (pGCL) of McIver and Morgan. Building on dynamic logic, pDL can express both first-order state properties and probabilistic reachability properties. In this paper, we report on work in progress towards a deductive proof system for pDL. This proof system, in line with verification systems for dynamic logic such as KeY, is based on forward reasoning by means of symbolic execution.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Johnsen, Einar Broch","Kamburjan, Eduard","Pardo, Raúl","Voogd, Erik","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789552"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Deductive verification","Dynamic logic","Probabilistic programs"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards a proof system for probabilistic dynamic logic","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2412.00906","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-789552","identifier":[{"id":"85212131535","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-60b7772c-cc33-47e0-86c8-3e09c609153f"],"keyword":["Deductive verification","Dynamic logic","Probabilistic programs"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B26DBC365B681C8CBCFADBFA76731EC6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2412.00906","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Einar Broch","key":"johnsenpau","last":"Johnsen","name":"Johnsen, Einar Broch","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eduard","key":"kamburjanpau","last":"Kamburjan","name":"Kamburjan, Eduard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Raul","key":"pardopau","last":"Pardo","locid":"d05daa00-c3d6-4a89-ba14-cfd1847fb0cc","name":"Pardo, Raúl","name_org":"Pardo, Raul","orcid":"0000-0003-0003-7295","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"voogdpau","last":"Voogd","name":"Voogd, Erik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wąsowskipau","last":"Wąsowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","name_org":"Wąsowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-75783-9_13","pages":"322-338","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Towards a Proof System for Probabilistic Dynamic Logic","volume":"15260"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85212131535"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-60b7772c-cc33-47e0-86c8-3e09c609153f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards a Proof System for Probabilistic Dynamic Logic","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789552","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Autonomous Underwater Vehicles (AUVs) need to operate for days without human intervention and thus must be able to do efficient and reliable task planning. Unfortunately, efficient task planning requires deliberately abstract domain models (for scalability reasons), which in practice leads to plans that might be unreliable or under performing in practice. An optimal abstract plan may turn out suboptimal or unreliable during physical execution. To overcome this, we introduce a method that first generates a selection of diverse high-level plans and then assesses them in a low-level simulation to select the optimal and most reliable candidate. We evaluate the method using a realistic underwater robot simulation, estimating the risk metrics for different scenarios, demonstrating feasibility and effectiveness of the approach.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Mohammadi Kashani, Mahya","John, Tobias","Coffelt, Jeremy P.","Johnsen, Einar Broch","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776413"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Computer Science","Probabilistic planning","Risk Assessment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"risk averse planning and plan assessment for marine robots","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/107433497/2410.01018v1.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This project has received funding from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme under the Marie Skłodowska-Curie grant agreement No 956200 REMARO."],"id":"S01-000.00-776413","ids":["itu-72af3413-c476-4a58-be63-b8b62eb9d712"],"keyword":["Computer Science","marine robots","probabilistic planning","risk assessment","risk-averse planning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9702ED13F324867A991465C88234B370"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/107433497/2410.01018v1.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mahya Mohammadi","key":"kashanipau","last":"Kashani","locid":"fea53dc2-758b-4dc3-962c-68e0b52d2925","name":"Mohammadi Kashani, Mahya","name_org":"Kashani, Mahya Mohammadi","orcid":"0000-0001-7764-8268","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"johnpau","last":"John","name":"John, Tobias","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeremy P.","key":"coffeltpau","last":"Coffelt","name":"Coffelt, Jeremy P.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Einar Broch","key":"johnsenpau","last":"Johnsen","name":"Johnsen, Einar Broch","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-72af3413-c476-4a58-be63-b8b62eb9d712"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Risk-Averse Planning and Plan Assessment for Marine Robots","type":"Preprint","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776413","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"It is of utmost importance to ensure that modern data intensive systems do not leak sensitive information. In this paper, the authors, who met thanks to Joost-Pieter Katoen, discuss symbolic methods to compute information-theoretic measures of leakage: entropy, conditional entropy, Kullback-Leibler divergence, and mutual information. We build on two semantic frameworks for symbolic execution of probabilistic programs. For discrete programs, we use weakest pre-expectation calculus to compute exact symbolic expressions for the leakage measures. Using Second Order Gaussian Approximation (SOGA), we handle programs that combine discrete and continuous distributions. However, in the SOGA setting, we approximate the exact semantics using Gaussian mixtures and compute bounds for the measures. We demonstrate the use of our methods in two widely used mechanisms to ensure differential privacy: randomized response and the Gaussian mechanism.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Schröer, Philipp","Randone, Francesca","Pardo, Raúl","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-789555"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","RWTH Aachen University","Università degli studi di Trieste"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"symbolic quantitative information flow for probabilistic programs","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2412.00907","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-789555","identifier":[{"id":"85212081414","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6df74eae-62f6-46f9-bea0-7fa58224e923"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6C785A35686B1DD865C1946475BCD2F2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2412.00907","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"rwth aachen university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"RWTH Aachen University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"it","key":"università degli studi di trieste","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Università degli studi di Trieste","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Philipp","key":"schröerpau","last":"Schröer","name":"Schröer, Philipp","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Francesca","key":"randonepau","last":"Randone","name":"Randone, Francesca","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Raúl","key":"pardopau","last":"Pardo","locid":"d05daa00-c3d6-4a89-ba14-cfd1847fb0cc","name":"Pardo, Raúl","orcid":"0000-0003-0003-7295","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wa̧sowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","name_org":"Wa̧sowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-75783-9_6","pages":"128-154","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Symbolic Quantitative Information Flow for Probabilistic Programs","volume":"15260"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85212081414"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6df74eae-62f6-46f9-bea0-7fa58224e923"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Symbolic Quantitative Information Flow for Probabilistic Programs","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-789555","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Testing underwater vehicles in operational conditions is expensive. Formal models can lower the cost of operational testing and validation for these systems, as they allow detecting problems earlier. We propose modeling the underwater vehicle’s behavior as Timed Automata, and discuss examples of property patterns which can be handled by observer Timed Automata and Timed CTL properties. The goal is to build a set of specifications which can then be used for testing and validation of controllers in underwater vehicles.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Quijano, Sergio","Varshosaz, Mahsa","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-818239"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Control","Model based testing","Safety"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modeling and safety analysis of autonomous underwater vehicles behaviors","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85205990497","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This project has received funding from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme under the Marie Sklodowska-Curie grant agreement No 956200 REMARO, Reliable AI for Marine Robotics."],"id":"S01-000.00-818239","identifier":[{"id":"85205990497","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-54cb5410-342b-4b42-b37c-8c48b63e83aa"],"keyword":["Model-based testing","Safety","autonomous underwater robots","control"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-782E16DA0A2E62010F50CB0315AA07C8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sergio","key":"quijanopau","last":"Quijano","locid":"fc57a764-276e-463a-aa68-fa54ffaf31d6","name":"Quijano, Sergio","orcid":"0000-0002-2138-9946","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mahsa","key":"varshosazpau","last":"Varshosaz","locid":"fb4b9d17-f1ec-466b-b222-caba06823edc","name":"Varshosaz, Mahsa","orcid":"0000-0002-4776-883X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icstw60967.2024.00022","eisbn":["9798350344790"],"status":"p","title":"2024 IEEE International Conference on Software Testing, Verification and Validation Workshops"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85205990497"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-54cb5410-342b-4b42-b37c-8c48b63e83aa"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Modeling and Safety Analysis of Autonomous Underwater Vehicles Behaviors","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-818239","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper addresses the challenges posed by urban stormwater runoff in light of increased urbanization and climate change, which strain traditional stormwater infrastructure. It focuses on mitigating Combined Sewer Overflows (CSOs) by maximizing urban runoff storage in stormwater tunnels during Wastewater Treatment Plant (WWTP) capacity overloads. Unlike passive rule-based control, this research explores adaptive control systems that utilize weather forecasts and dynamic strategies. It introduces a novel control synthesis approach, combining Model Predictive Control (MPC) and Q-learning, to optimize CSO management based on real-time weather predictions. Simulated evaluations (using EPA-SWMM, focused on the Hvidovre stormwater tunnel in Copenhagen, Denmark) show significant improvements in CSO management: 17% over classic Q-learning and 34% over Q-learning with the \\uppaal model, and 72% over Rule-Based Control (RBC). Our method, MPC Q-learning, dynamically incorporates weather conditions, outperforming other Q-learning approaches.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Kim, Esther Hahyeon","Nielsen, Thomas Dyhre","Larsen, Kim Guldstrand","Goorden, Martijn","Ghaffari, Mohsen","Wasowski, Andrzej","Høeg-Petersen, Andreas Holck"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-743453"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Combined sewer overflows","Control synthesis","Model predictive control","Reinforcement learning","Stormwater management"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"minimizing combined sewer overflows with online model predictive reinforcement learning","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"funding_acknowledgement":["DIREC - Innovation fund"],"id":"S01-000.00-743453","ids":["aau-ff1fe156-5dff-4b3b-849b-1467d8624168"],"keyword":["Combined sewer overflows","Control synthesis","Model predictive control","Reinforcement learning","Stormwater management,"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-BC69F708D25763563BE1285CBAAA733A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Distributed, Embedded and Intelligent Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Esther Hahyeon","key":"kimpau","last":"Kim","locid":"b5e4baa3-b733-4458-8c7d-e2cafa731be9","name":"Kim, Esther Hahyeon","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Dyhre","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d815ae40-14ed-44a2-a215-172e83022c8e","name":"Nielsen, Thomas Dyhre","orcid":"0000-0002-4823-6341","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim Guldstrand","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"27dbc400-17ea-4672-9343-63093ad486c9","name":"Larsen, Kim Guldstrand","orcid":"0000-0002-5953-3384","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martijn","key":"goordenpau","last":"Goorden","locid":"d71e2c9c-86de-43d9-b98b-2d204bd7a9fa","name":"Goorden, Martijn","orcid":"0000-0002-0641-7240","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohsen","key":"ghaffaripau","last":"Ghaffari","name":"Ghaffari, Mohsen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas Holck","key":"høegpetersenpau","last":"Høeg-Petersen","locid":"c4ec89d5-fd6a-4cdd-b7a5-9a6415f34f64","name":"Høeg-Petersen, Andreas Holck","orcid":"0009-0003-7829-7318","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"journal":"Journal - in the process","pages":"1-18","status":"s","title":"Journal - in the process"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["13. Climate Action","6. Clean Water and Sanitation","9. Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Submitted"]},"sid":["aau-ff1fe156-5dff-4b3b-849b-1467d8624168"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Minimizing Combined Sewer Overflows with Online Model-Predictive Reinforcement Learning","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-743453","year":"2024","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Labeling images for every new task or data pattern a model needs to learn is a significant time bottleneck in real-world applications. Moreover, acquiring the necessary data for training the models can be challenging. Ideally, one would train the models with simulated images and adapt them for the desired real tasks using the least possible amount of data. Active learning can be used to solve this problem with minimal effort. In this work, we train SegFormer for pipeline segmentation with synthetic images from an underwater simulated environment and fine-tune the model with real underwater pipeline images recorded in a marina. The evaluation shows that selecting real data with active learning for fine-tuning the model gives better results than randomly selecting the images. As part of the work, we release the dataset recorded in the marina, MarinaPipe, which will be publicly available.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ribeiro Marnet, Luiza","Grasshof, Stella","Brodskiy, Yuri","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-764506"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Active learning","Computer vision","Image segmentation","Underwater inspection"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["EIVA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bridging the sim to real gap for underwater image segmentation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"funding_acknowledgement":["funding from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme under the Marie Skłodowska-Curie grant agreement No. 956200"],"id":"S01-000.00-764506","identifier":[{"id":"85206447240","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4be18a27-833b-4475-944f-6314d0445bcf"],"keyword":["Underwater inspection","active learning","computer vision","image segmentation","sim-to-real"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-FB6E8E748F7A58E12007FA6000723D75"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["EIVA"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Audio-Visual Computing","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Luiza","key":"ribeiromarnetpau","last":"Ribeiro Marnet","name":"Ribeiro Marnet, Luiza","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stella","key":"graßhofpau","last":"Graßhof","locid":"ad50bed7-77fd-4c7f-819c-54455506e3f0","name":"Grasshof, Stella","name_org":"Graßhof, Stella","orcid":"0000-0002-6791-7425","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuri","key":"brodskiypau","last":"Brodskiy","name":"Brodskiy, Yuri","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["itu-4be18a27-833b-4475-944f-6314d0445bcf"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Bridging the Sim-to-Real GAP for Underwater Image Segmentation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-764506","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Data analysis has high value both for commercial and research purposes. However, disclosing analysis results may pose severe privacy risk to individuals. Privug is a method to quantify privacy risks of data analytics programs by analyzing their source code. The method uses probability distributions to model attacker knowledge and Bayesian inference to update said knowledge based on observable outputs. Currently, Privug uses Markov Chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) to perform inference, which is a flexible but approximate solution. This paper presents an exact Bayesian inference engine based on multivariate Gaussian distributions to accurately and efficiently quantify privacy risks. The inference engine is implemented for a subset of Python programs that can be modeled as multivariate Gaussian models. We evaluate the method by analyzing privacy risks in programs to release public statistics. The evaluation shows that our method accurately and efficiently analyzes privacy risks, and outperforms existing methods. Furthermore, we demonstrate the use of our engine to analyze the effect of differential privacy in public statistics.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Rønneberg, Rasmus Carl","Pardo, Raúl","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712539"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karlsruhe Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Bayesian inference","Data analysis","Differential Privacy","Markov chain Monte Carlo","Privacy risks"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exact and efficient bayesian inference for privacy risk quantification","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102015577/pre-print-sefm2023-ronneberg-pardo-wasowski.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-712539","identifier":[{"id":"85177449213","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-9453cea8-9b66-4bf8-9aab-611805efae7b"],"keyword":["Bayesian inference","Data analysis","Differential privacy","Markov Chain Monte Carlo","Privacy risks"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-28231623076AF80A32B4598B7A2522C1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102015577/pre-print-sefm2023-ronneberg-pardo-wasowski.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"karlsruhe institute of technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Karlsruhe Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus Carl","key":"rønnebergpau","last":"Rønneberg","name":"Rønneberg, Rasmus Carl","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Raúl","key":"pardopau","last":"Pardo","locid":"d05daa00-c3d6-4a89-ba14-cfd1847fb0cc","name":"Pardo, Raúl","orcid":"0000-0003-0003-7295","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-47115-5_15","eisbn":["9783031471155"],"isbn":["9783031471148"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"263-281","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of Software Engineering and Formal Methods (SEFM'23)","volume":"14323"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85177449213"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-9453cea8-9b66-4bf8-9aab-611805efae7b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exact and Efficient Bayesian Inference for Privacy Risk Quantification","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-712539","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Varshosaz, Mahsa","Ghaffari, Mohsen","Broch Johnsen, Einar","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718913"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards formal specification of reinforcement learning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-718913","ids":["itu-c1a10abd-9db2-4146-815d-57736cc40085"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E5D2FB9830E288FC9C228A74AAE03914"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mahsa","key":"varshosazpau","last":"Varshosaz","locid":"fb4b9d17-f1ec-466b-b222-caba06823edc","name":"Varshosaz, Mahsa","orcid":"0000-0002-4776-883X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohsen","key":"ghaffaripau","last":"Ghaffari","locid":"c12518ce-b3ab-469c-81fb-e2178e6b87e3","name":"Ghaffari, Mohsen","orcid":"0000-0002-1939-9053","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Einar","key":"brochjohnsenpau","last":"Broch Johnsen","name":"Broch Johnsen, Einar","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c1a10abd-9db2-4146-815d-57736cc40085"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards Formal Specification of Reinforcement Learning","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718913","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Software bots fulfill an important role in collective software development, and their adoption by developers promises increased productivity.  Past research has identified that bots that communicate too often can irritate developers, which affects the utility of the bot. However, it is not clear what other properties of human-bot collaboration affect developers' preferences, or what impact these properties might have. The main idea of this paper is to explore characteristics affecting developer preferences for interactions between humans and bots, in the context of GitHub pull requests.  We carried out an exploratory sequential study with interviews and a subsequent vignette-based survey. We find developers generally prefer bots that are personable but show little autonomy, however, more experienced developers tend to prefer more autonomous bots. Based on this empirical evidence, we recommend bot developers increase configuration options for bots so that individual developers and projects can configure bots to best align with their own preferences and project cultures.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Ghorbani, Amir","Cassee, Nathan","Robinson, Derek","Alami, Adam","Ernst, Neil A.","Serebrenik, Alexander","Wąsowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S02-082.76-715818"],"event":{"end":"2023-05-20","start":"2023-05-14","title":"International Conference on Software Engineering (ICSE)","year":"2023"},"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Eindhoven University of Technology","University of Victoria","University of Victoria BC"],"keyword":["Human Aspects","Human Aspects of Software Engineering","Open source software","Pull Request","Software Bot"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"autonomy is an acquired taste exploring developer preferences for github bots","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102814271/2023-icse-bots.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-082.76-715818","identifier":[{"id":"85171733481","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f278a9bf-8c94-4909-80c1-06ed570015e6","itu-f7a52ce2-7652-4523-8d85-fa2556141612"],"keyword":["Human Aspects","Human Aspects of Software Engineering","Open source software","Pull Request","Software Bot"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-322289F948368FE0DBEFBA6AE643F018"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102814271/2023-icse-bots.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ca","key":"university of victoria bc","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Victoria BC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"university of victoria","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Victoria","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"eindhoven university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Eindhoven University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centered Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Amir","key":"ghorbanipau","last":"Ghorbani","name":"Ghorbani, Amir","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nathan","key":"casseepau","last":"Cassee","name":"Cassee, Nathan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Derek","key":"robinsonpau","last":"Robinson","name":"Robinson, Derek","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Adam","key":"alamipau","last":"Alami","locid":"ef3cb54e-65d7-4493-9bbe-2ae5cc274b2e","name":"Alami, Adam","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Neil A.","key":"ernstpau","last":"Ernst","name":"Ernst, Neil A.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander","key":"serebrenikpau","last":"Serebrenik","name":"Serebrenik, Alexander","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icse48619.2023.00123","eisbn":["9781665457019"],"isbn":["9781665457026"],"issn":["02705257","15581225"],"issn_org":["02705257"],"journal":"Proceedings of the International Conference on Software Engineering","pages":"1405-1417","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the International Conference on Software Engineering","volume":"2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85171733481"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f278a9bf-8c94-4909-80c1-06ed570015e6","itu-f7a52ce2-7652-4523-8d85-fa2556141612"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Autonomy Is An Acquired Taste: Exploring Developer Preferences for GitHub Bots","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-082.76-715818","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"This textbook describes the theory and the pragmatics of using and engineering high-level software languages – also known as modeling or domain-specific languages (DSLs) – for creating quality software. This includes methods, design patterns, guidelines, and testing practices for defining the syntax and the semantics of languages. While remaining close to technology, the book covers multiple paradigms and solutions, avoiding a particular technological silo. It unifies the modeling, the object-oriented, and the functional-programming perspectives on DSLs. The book has 13 chapters. Chapters 1 and 2 introduce and motivate DSLs. Chapter 3 kicks off the DSL engineering lifecycle, describing how to systematically develop abstract syntax by analyzing a domain. Chapter 4 addresses the concrete syntax, including the systematic engineering of context-free grammars. Chapters 5 and 6 cover the static semantics – with basic constraints as a starting point and type systems for advanced DSLs. Chapters 7 (Transformation), 8 (Interpretation), and 9 (Generation) describe different paradigms for designing and implementing the dynamic semantics, while covering testing and other kinds of quality assurance. Chapter 10 is devoted to internal DSLs. Chapters 11 to 13 show the application of DSLs and engage with simpler alternatives to DSLs in a highly distinguished domain: software variability. These chapters introduce the underlying notions of software product lines and feature modeling. The book has been developed based on courses on model-driven software engineering (MDSE) and DSLs held by the authors. It aims at senior undergraduate and junior graduate students in computer science or software engineering. Since it includes examples and lessons from industrial and open-source projects, as well as from industrial research, practitioners will also find it a useful reference. The numerous examples include code in Scala 3, ATL, Alloy, C#, F#, Groovy, Java, JavaScript, Kotlin, OCL, Python, QVT, Ruby, and Xtend. The book contains as many as 277 exercises. The associated code repository facilitates learning and using the examples in a course.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Wasowski, Andrzej","Berger, Thorsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384847"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Ruhr University Bochum"],"keyword":["Domain Specific Languages DSLs","Model Driven Software Engineering MDSE","Software Variability","Syntax and Semantics","Testing and Quality Assurance"],"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"domain specific languages effective modeling automation and reuse","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.barnesandnoble.com/w/domain-specific-languages-andrzej-wasowski/1142696306","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384847","ids":["itu-f3596c05-28e1-4fa8-a23a-ca3f648a238f"],"keyword":["Domain-Specific Languages (DSLs)","Model-Driven Software Engineering (MDSE)","Software Variability","Syntax and Semantics","Testing and Quality Assurance"],"lang":"English","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-52BF9C3265971AD12F1AA36F91069F18"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"ruhr university bochum","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ruhr University Bochum","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thorsten","key":"bergerpau","last":"Berger","name":"Berger, Thorsten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9783031236686"],"pages":"492","publisher":"Springer","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","scoID":["2-s2.0-85161848405"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f3596c05-28e1-4fa8-a23a-ca3f648a238f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Domain-Specific Languages : Effective modeling, automation, and reuse","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384847","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"We present a new symbolic execution semantics of probabilistic programs that include observe statements and sampling from continuous distributions. Building on Kozen’s seminal work, this symbolic semantics consists of a countable collection of measurable functions, along with a partition of the state space. We use the new semantics to provide a full correctness proof of symbolic execution for probabilistic programs. We also implement this semantics in the tool symProb, and illustrate its use on examples.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Voogd, Erik","Broch Johnsen, Einar","Silva, Alexandra","Susag, Zachary J.","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712560"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cornell University","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Continuous Distributions","Observe Statements","Probabilistic programs","SymProb Tool","Symbolic execution"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"symbolic semantics for probabilistic programs","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2307.09951.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-712560","identifier":[{"id":"85174271638","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ddafa298-f2f8-4a42-8ac9-1460b033560b"],"keyword":["Continuous Distributions","Observe Statements","Probabilistic Programs","SymProb Tool","Symbolic Execution"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-750CEA3B6BDE81B38707205A518A1FE9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2307.09951.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"cornell university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cornell University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"voogdpau","last":"Voogd","name":"Voogd, Erik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Einar","key":"brochjohnsenpau","last":"Broch Johnsen","name":"Broch Johnsen, Einar","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexandra","key":"silvapau","last":"Silva","name":"Silva, Alexandra","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Zachary J.","key":"susagpau","last":"Susag","name":"Susag, Zachary J.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2307.09951","issn":["03029743"],"issue":"QEST","pages":"329-345","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"Quantitative Evaluation of Systems 20th International Conference, QEST 2023, Antwerp, Belgium, September 20–22, 2023, Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85174271638"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ddafa298-f2f8-4a42-8ac9-1460b033560b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Symbolic Semantics for Probabilistic Programs","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-712560","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Self-adaptation can be used in robotics to increase system robust- ness and reliability. This work describes the Metacontrol method for self-adaptation in robotics. Particularly, it details how the MROS (Metacontrol for ROS Systems) framework implements and pack- ages Metacontrol, and it demonstrate how MROS can be applied in a navigation scenario where a mobile robot navigates in a factory floor. Video: https://www.youtube.com/watchvISe9aMskJuE","author_count":8,"contributors":["Rezende Silva, Gustavo","Garcia, Nadia Hammoudeh","Bozhinoski, Darko","Deshpande, Harshavardhan","Oviedo, Mario Garzon","Wasowski, Andrzej","Ramírez Montero, Mariano","Corbato, Carlos Hernandez"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718885"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Germany","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Delft University of Technology","Fraunhofer Institute for Manufacturing Engineering and Automation IPA","University Libre du Bruxelles"],"keyword":["Floors","Mobile robots","Navigation","Production facilities","Reliability","Software Engineering"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mros a framework for robot self adaptation","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2303.09227.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718885","identifier":[{"id":"85171880084","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8a018f95-2956-45e5-b4a1-782266c02b5e"],"keyword":["Floors","Mobile robots","Navigation","Production facilities","Reliability","Software engineering"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-38C7C10EC638BFA23A2BB47F284FA5A0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2303.09227.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"delft university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Delft University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"fraunhofer institute for manufacturing engineering and automation ipa","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Fraunhofer Institute for Manufacturing Engineering and Automation IPA","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"be","key":"university libre du bruxelles","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Libre du Bruxelles","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gustavo","key":"rezendesilvapau","last":"Rezende Silva","name":"Rezende Silva, Gustavo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nadia Hammoudeh","key":"garciapau","last":"Garcia","name":"Garcia, Nadia Hammoudeh","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Darko","key":"bozhinoskipau","last":"Bozhinoski","name":"Bozhinoski, Darko","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Harshavardhan","key":"deshpandepau","last":"Deshpande","name":"Deshpande, Harshavardhan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mario Garzon","key":"oviedopau","last":"Oviedo","name":"Oviedo, Mario Garzon","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mariano","key":"ramírezmonteropau","last":"Ramírez Montero","name":"Ramírez Montero, Mariano","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carlos Hernandez","key":"corbatopau","last":"Corbato","name":"Corbato, Carlos Hernandez","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/icse-companion58688.2023.00044","eisbn":["9798350322637"],"place":"Melbourne","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2023 IEEE/ACM 45th International Conference on Software Engineering: Companion Proceedings (ICSE-Companion)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85171880084"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8a018f95-2956-45e5-b4a1-782266c02b5e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"MROS: A framework for robot self-adaptation","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718885","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Robots in many domains need to plan and make decisions under uncertainty; for example, autonomous underwater vehicles (AUVs) gathering data in environments inaccessible to humans, need to perform automated task planning. Planning problems are typically solved by risk-neutral optimization maximizing a single objective, such as limited time or energy consumption. A typical probabilistic planner synthesizes a plan to reach the desired goals with a maximum expected reward, given the possible initial states and actions of the world. In this work, we additionally consider risk metrics for selecting solutions to such planning problems. Consider a marine robotics mission scenario where the task is to survey pipeline segments safely based on various risk measurements.","author_count":5,"contributors":["John, Tobias","Mohammadi Kashani, Mahya","P Coffelt, Jeremy","Broch Johnsen, Einar","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718938"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bremen, Research and Technology Group","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Marine Robotics","Planning","Reliability engineering","Risk Assessment"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reliable plan selection with quantified risk sensitivity","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"GNU GPL","type":"rem","url":"https://mdu.drive.sunet.se/index.php/s/srKL2LDAF369mZt","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-718938","ids":["itu-fe546730-7e37-4f20-bf85-2ad15813058a"],"keyword":["Planning","Reliability engineering","marine robotics","risk assessment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7A1DAA470924887F4318F2AD1924FA57"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"GNU GPL","type":"rem","url":"https://mdu.drive.sunet.se/index.php/s/srKL2LDAF369mZt","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"bremen research and technology group","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Bremen, Research and Technology Group","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"johnpau","last":"John","name":"John, Tobias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mahya","key":"mohammadikashanipau","last":"Mohammadi Kashani","locid":"fea53dc2-758b-4dc3-962c-68e0b52d2925","name":"Mohammadi Kashani, Mahya","orcid":"0000-0001-7764-8268","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeremy","key":"pcoffeltpau","last":"P Coffelt","name":"P Coffelt, Jeremy","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Einar","key":"brochjohnsenpau","last":"Broch Johnsen","name":"Broch Johnsen, Einar","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"NWPT 2023 - 34th Nordic Workshop on Programming Theory"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-fe546730-7e37-4f20-bf85-2ad15813058a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Reliable Plan Selection with Quantified Risk-Sensitivity","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718938","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"A specification theory combines notions of specifications and implementations with a satisfaction relation, a refinement relation and a set of operators supporting stepwise design. We develop a complete specification framework for real-time systems using Timed I/O Automata as the specification formalism, with the semantics expressed in terms of Timed I/O Transition Systems. We provide constructs for refinement, consistency checking, logical and structural composition, and quotient of specifications -- all indispensable ingredients of a compositional design methodology. The theory is backed by rigorous proofs and is being implemented in the open-source tool ECDAR.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Goorden, Martijn","Larsen, Kim Guldstrand","Legay, Axel","Lorber, Florian","Nyman, Ulrik","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-706097"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Université catholique de Louvain"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"timed i o automata it is never too late to complete your timed specification theory","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dpr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/ARXIV.2302.04529","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-706097","ids":["aau-e506413a-43d7-4b1f-bb7b-1dbe8b6b1bcf"],"lang":"Undetermined","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-69DAA3C8E0B0D3E21AC5D578400C3104"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.48550/ARXIV.2302.04529","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/645428162/Timed_IO_Automata_It_is_never_too_late_to_complete.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Distributed, Embedded and Intelligent Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"be","key":"université catholique de louvain","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Université catholique de Louvain","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martijn A.","key":"goordenpau","last":"Goorden","locid":"d71e2c9c-86de-43d9-b98b-2d204bd7a9fa","name":"Goorden, Martijn","name_org":"Goorden, Martijn A.","orcid":"0000-0002-0641-7240","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim G.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"27dbc400-17ea-4672-9343-63093ad486c9","name":"Larsen, Kim Guldstrand","name_org":"Larsen, Kim G.","orcid":"0000-0002-5953-3384","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Axel","key":"legaypau","last":"Legay","name":"Legay, Axel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Florian","key":"lorberpau","last":"Lorber","locid":"b66b0314-083f-4d48-b8f2-e7481adb792e","name":"Lorber, Florian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulrik","key":"nymanpau","last":"Nyman","locid":"bbb0f361-fbbd-4e7b-88fb-e40c75e5ecdd","name":"Nyman, Ulrik","orcid":"0000-0001-6430-540X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.48550/arxiv.2302.04529","publisher":"arXiv","status":"p","volume":"2302.04529"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e506413a-43d7-4b1f-bb7b-1dbe8b6b1bcf"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Timed I/O Automata : It is never too late to complete your timed specification theory","type":"Preprint","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-706097","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Autonomous robots combine skills to form increasingly complex behaviors, called missions. While skills are often programmed at a relatively low abstraction level, their coordination is architecturally separated and often expressed in higher-level languages or frameworks. State machines have been the go-to language to model behavior for decades, but recently, behavior trees have gained attention among roboticists. Originally designed to model autonomous actors in computer games, behavior trees offer an extensible tree-based representation of missions and are claimed to support modular design and code reuse. Although several implementations of behavior trees are in use, little is known about their usage and scope in the real world. How do concepts offered by behavior trees relate to traditional languages, such as state machines? How are concepts in behavior trees and state machines used in actual applications? This paper is a study of the key language concepts in behavior trees as realized in domain-specific languages (DSLs), internal and external DSLs offered as libraries, and their use in open-source robotic applications supported by the Robot Operating System (ROS). We analyze behavior-tree DSLs and compare them to the standard language for behavior models in robotics: state machines. We identify DSLs for both behavior-modeling languages, and we analyze five in-depth. We mine open-source repositories for robotic applications that use the analyzed DSLs and analyze their usage. We identify similarities between behavior trees and state machines in terms of language design and the concepts offered to accommodate the needs of the robotics domain. We observed that the usage of behavior-tree DSLs in open-source projects is increasing rapidly. We observed similar usage patterns at model structure and at code reuse in the behavior-tree and state-machine models within the mined open-source projects. We contribute all extracted models as a dataset, hoping to inspire the community to use and further develop behavior trees, associated tools, and analysis techniques.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Ghzouli, Razan","Berger, Thorsten","Broch Johnsen, Einar","Wasowski, Andrzej","Dragule, Swaib"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718879"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chalmers University of Technology","Ruhr University Bochum","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Behavior Trees","Empirical study","State Machines","robotics applications","usage patterns"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"behavior trees and state machines in robotics applications","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102814099/Behaviour_Trees_and_State_Machines_in_Robotics_Applications.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718879","identifier":[{"id":"85153799502","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-85a3a74c-5fdb-4184-8738-b16dacaeafb9"],"keyword":["behavior trees","empirical study","robotics applications","state machines","usage patterns"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0C70B302CDE2AC75ED8CC310E4BA0CAA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102814099/Behaviour_Trees_and_State_Machines_in_Robotics_Applications.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2208.04211.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"chalmers university of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Chalmers University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"ruhr university bochum","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ruhr University Bochum","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Razan","key":"ghzoulipau","last":"Ghzouli","name":"Ghzouli, Razan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thorsten","key":"bergerpau","last":"Berger","name":"Berger, Thorsten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Einar","key":"brochjohnsenpau","last":"Broch Johnsen","name":"Broch Johnsen, Einar","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Swaib","key":"dragulepau","last":"Dragule","name":"Dragule, Swaib","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/tse.2023.3269081","issn":["00985589","19393520"],"issn_org":["00985589"],"issue":"9","journal":"IEEE Transactions on Software Engineering","pages":"4243-4267","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"IEEE Transactions on Software Engineering","title_org":"I E E E Transactions on Software Engineering","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85153799502"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-85a3a74c-5fdb-4184-8738-b16dacaeafb9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Behavior Trees and State Machines in Robotics Applications","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718879","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The development process for reinforcement learning applications is still exploratory rather than systematic. This exploratory nature reduces reuse of specifications between applications and increases the chances of introducing programming errors. This paper takes a step towards systematizing the development of reinforcement learning applications. We introduce a formal specification of reinforcement learning problems and algorithms, with a particular focus on temporal difference methods and their definitions in backup diagrams. We further develop a test harness for a large class of reinforcement learning applications based on temporal difference learning, including SARSA and Q-learning. The entire development is rooted in functional programming methods; starting with pure specifications and denotational semantics, ending with property-based testing and using compositional interpreters for a domain-specific term language as a test oracle for concrete implementations. We demonstrate the usefulness of this testing method on a number of examples, and evaluate with mutation testing. We show that our test suite is effective in killing mutants (90% mutants killed for 75% of subject agents). More importantly, almost half of all mutants are killed by generic write-once-use-everywhere tests that apply to any reinforcement learning problem modeled using our library, without any additional effort from the programmer.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Varshosaz, Mahsa","Ghaffari, Mohsen","Broch Johnsen, Einar","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-718929"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["Program specifications","Software testing and debugging","Theory of computation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"formal specification and testing for reinforcement learning","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3607835","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-718929","identifier":[{"id":"85170641997","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e1a419da-e1e2-4370-82df-ef6d760dcef4"],"keyword":["Program specifications","Software testing and debugging","Theory of computation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-57A3A50D8022ABBDAEC486C17E7459DE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3607835","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/102788488/23-icfp.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mahsa","key":"varshosazpau","last":"Varshosaz","locid":"fb4b9d17-f1ec-466b-b222-caba06823edc","name":"Varshosaz, Mahsa","orcid":"0000-0002-4776-883X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohsen","key":"ghaffaripau","last":"Ghaffari","locid":"c12518ce-b3ab-469c-81fb-e2178e6b87e3","name":"Ghaffari, Mohsen","orcid":"0000-0002-1939-9053","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Einar","key":"brochjohnsenpau","last":"Broch Johnsen","name":"Broch Johnsen, Einar","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3607835","issn":["24751421"],"issue":"Issue ICFP","journal":"Proceedings of the ACM on Programming Languages","pages":"125-158","paperid":"193","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the ACM on Programming Languages","volume":"7"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-85170641997"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e1a419da-e1e2-4370-82df-ef6d760dcef4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Formal Specification and Testing for Reinforcement Learning","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718929","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The Linux Kernel is a world-class operating system controlling most of our computing infrastructure: mobile devices, Internet routers and services, and most of the supercomputers. Linux is also an example of low-level software with no comprehensive regression test suite (for good reasons). The kernel's tremendous societal importance imposes strict stability and correctness requirements. These properties make Linux a challenging and relevant target for static automated program repair (APR). Over the last decade, a significant progress has been made in dynamic APR. However, dynamic APR techniques do not translate naturally to systems without tests. We present a static APR technique addressing sequential locking API misuse bugs in the Linux Kernel. We attack the key challenge of static APR, namely the lack of detailed program specification, by combining static analysis with machine learning to complement the information presented by the static analyzer. In experiments on historical real-world bugs in the kernel, we were able to automatically re-produce or propose equivalent patches in 85% of the human made patches, and automatically rank them among the top three candidates for 64% of the cases and among the top five for 74%.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Cruz, Alfredo","Varshosaz, Mahsa","Le Goues, Claire","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382107"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Carnegie Mellon University"],"keyword":["Automatic Program Repair","Bugs"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patching locking bugs statically with crayons","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3548684","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382107","identifier":[{"id":"85162003734","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-390a76e2-8df8-4f47-a492-3f53d89714bd"],"keyword":["Automatic Program Repair","Bugs"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5E793693139BFD8F2F8392EB6E39C492"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3548684","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3548684","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/101336666/3548684.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"carnegie mellon university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Carnegie Mellon University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alfredo","key":"cruzpau","last":"Cruz","name":"Cruz, Alfredo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mahsa","key":"varshosazpau","last":"Varshosaz","locid":"fb4b9d17-f1ec-466b-b222-caba06823edc","name":"Varshosaz, Mahsa","orcid":"0000-0002-4776-883X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Claire","key":"legouespau","last":"Le Goues","name":"Le Goues, Claire","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3548684","issn":["1049331X","15577392"],"issn_org":["1049331X"],"journal":"ACM Transactions on Software Engineering and Methodology","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ACM Transactions on Software Engineering and Methodology"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85162003734"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-390a76e2-8df8-4f47-a492-3f53d89714bd"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Patching Locking Bugs Statically with Crayons","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382107","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The semantics of probabilistic languages has been extensively studied, but specification languages for their properties have received little attention. This paper introduces the probabilistic dynamic logic pDL, a specification logic for programs in the probabilistic guarded command language (pGCL) of McIver and Morgan. The proposed logic pDL can express both first-order state properties and probabilistic reachability properties, addressing both the non-deterministic and probabilistic choice operators of pGCL. In order to precisely explain the meaning of specifications, we formally define the satisfaction relation for pDL. Since pDL embeds pGCL programs in its box-modality operator, pDL satisfiability builds on a formal MDP semantics for pGCL programs. The satisfaction relation is modeled after PCTL, but extended from propositional to first-order setting of dynamic logic, and also embedding program fragments. We study basic properties of pDL, such as weakening and distribution, that can support reasoning systems. Finally, we demonstrate the use of pDL to reason about program behavior.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Pardo, Raúl","Broch Johnsen, Einar","Schaefer, Ina","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382634"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karlsruhe Institute of Technology","University of Oslo"],"keyword":["First Order State Properties","Markov decision processes","Probabilistic Dynamic Logic","Probabilistic Guarded Command Language","Probabilistic Reachability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a specification logic for programs in the probabilistic guarded command language","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90364299/22_ictac_preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-382634","identifier":[{"id":"85140773196","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5bb0e63b-d32f-479b-9961-ed759f0bc6ed"],"keyword":["First-Order State Properties","Markov Decision Processes","Probabilistic Dynamic Logic","Probabilistic Guarded Command Language","Probabilistic Reachability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AE46A1F9620A256FFD4AD2B13A4A9976"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/90364299/22_ictac_preprint.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2205.04822.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"karlsruhe institute of technology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Karlsruhe Institute of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Raúl","key":"pardopau","last":"Pardo","locid":"d05daa00-c3d6-4a89-ba14-cfd1847fb0cc","name":"Pardo, Raúl","orcid":"0000-0003-0003-7295","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Einar","key":"brochjohnsenpau","last":"Broch Johnsen","name":"Broch Johnsen, Einar","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ina","key":"schaeferpau","last":"Schaefer","name":"Schaefer, Ina","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-17715-6_24","eisbn":["9783031177156"],"isbn":["9783031177149"],"publisher":"Springer","series":"Proceedings of 19th International Colloquium on Theoretical Aspects of Computing - ICTAC","status":"p","title":"A Specification Logic for Programs in the Probabilistic Guarded Command Language","volume":"13572"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140773196"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5bb0e63b-d32f-479b-9961-ed759f0bc6ed"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Specification Logic for Programs in the Probabilistic Guarded Command Language","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382634","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"We propose a framework expanding the capabilities of underwater robots to autonomously recover from anomalous situations. The framework is built around a knowledge model developed in three stages. First, we create a deterministic knowledge base to describe the “health” of hardware, software, and environment components involved in a mission. Next, we describe the same components probabilistically, defining probabilities of failures, faults, and fixes. Finally, we combine the deterministic and probabilistic knowledge into a minimal ROS package designed to detect failures, isolate the underlying faults, propose fixes for the faults, and determine which is the most likely to help. We motivate the solution with a camera fault scenario and demonstrate it with a thruster failure on a real AUV and a simulated ROV.","author_count":3,"contributors":["no-lastname, no-firstname","Mohammadi Kashani, Mahya","Wasowski, Andrzej","no-lastname, no-firstname"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384375"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","ROSEN Research and Technology Group"],"keyword":["Marine Robotics","fault detection and recovery","ontology based autonomy","probabilistic logic programming"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"belief based fault recovery for marine robotics","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-3249/paper3-RobOntics.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384375","ids":["itu-d371a84b-cf7a-4e79-84ce-90b3c1008870"],"keyword":["fault detection and recovery","marine robotics","ontology-based autonomy","probabilistic logic programming"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A04EB1754C49F5A8449D0B5B22879F6E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"http://ceur-ws.org/Vol-3249/paper3-RobOntics.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"rosen research and technology group","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"ROSEN Research and Technology Group","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"no-firstname","key":"nolastnamenofirstnamepau","last":"no-lastname","name":"no-lastname, no-firstname","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mahya","key":"mohammadikashanimahyapau","last":"Mohammadi Kashani","locid":"fea53dc2-758b-4dc3-962c-68e0b52d2925","name":"Mohammadi Kashani, Mahya","orcid":"0000-0001-7764-8268","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskiandrzejpau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p","title":"The Eighth Joint Ontology Workshops (JOWO’22), August 15-19, 2022, Jönköping University, Sweden","volume":"Vol-3249"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d371a84b-cf7a-4e79-84ce-90b3c1008870"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Belief-based fault recovery for marine robotics","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384375","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Known attempts to build autonomous robots rely on complex control architectures, usually implemented with the Robot Operating System (ROS). Runtime adaptation is needed in these systems, to cope with component failures and with contingencies arising from dynamic environments – otherwise these affect the reliability and quality of the mission execution. Existing proposals on how to build self-adaptive systems in robotics usually require a major re-design of the control architecture and rely on complex tools unfamiliar to the robotics community. Moreover, they are hard to reuse across applications. This paper presents MROS: a model-based framework for runtime adaptation of robot control architectures based on ROS. MROS uses a combination of domain-specific languages to model architectural variants and capture mission quality concerns, and an ontology-based implementation of the MAPE-K and meta-control visions for runtime adaptation. The experiment results obtained applying MROS in two realistic ROS-based robotic demonstrators show the benefits of our approach in terms of the quality of the mission execution, and MROS's extensibility and reusability across robotic applications.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bozhinoski, Darko","Oviedo, Mario Garzon","Garcia, Nadia Hammoudeh","Deshpande, Harshavardhan","Hoorn, Gijs van der","Tjerngren, Jon","Wasowski, Andrzej","Corbato, Carlos Hernández"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384185"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands","Sweden"],"glorg":["ABB Corporate Research Center","All Global Affiliations","Delft University of Technology","Fraunhofer Institute for Manufacturing Engineering and Automation IPA"],"keyword":["Autonomous robots","Control architecture","Ontologies","Self Adaptive Systems","Variability","models at runtime"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mros runtime adaptation for robot control architectures","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92076647/2022_bozhinoski_mros_runtime_adaptation_journal.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384185","identifier":[{"id":"85126021315","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-c6cbcc3e-3e48-4a5e-b51d-aff17acfe183"],"keyword":[": self-adaptive systems","autonomous robots","control architecture","models-at-runtime","ontologies","variability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AD919186FF584A68EA3D3BCEB042C5BA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/92076647/2022_bozhinoski_mros_runtime_adaptation_journal.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"delft university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Delft University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"fraunhofer institute for manufacturing engineering and automation ipa","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Fraunhofer Institute for Manufacturing Engineering and Automation IPA","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"abb corporate research center","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ABB Corporate Research Center","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Darko","key":"bozhinoskipau","last":"Bozhinoski","name":"Bozhinoski, Darko","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mario Garzon","key":"oviedopau","last":"Oviedo","name":"Oviedo, Mario Garzon","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nadia Hammoudeh","key":"garciapau","last":"Garcia","name":"Garcia, Nadia Hammoudeh","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Harshavardhan","key":"deshpandepau","last":"Deshpande","name":"Deshpande, Harshavardhan","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Gijs van der","key":"hoornpau","last":"Hoorn","name":"Hoorn, Gijs van der","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jon","key":"tjerngrenpau","last":"Tjerngren","name":"Tjerngren, Jon","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carlos Hernández","key":"corbatopau","last":"Corbato","name":"Corbato, Carlos Hernández","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/01691864.2022.2039761","issn":["01691864","15685535"],"issn_org":["01691864"],"issue":"11","journal":"Advanced Robotics","pages":"502-518","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Advanced Robotics","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85126021315"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-c6cbcc3e-3e48-4a5e-b51d-aff17acfe183"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"MROS: runtime adaptation for robot control architectures","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384185","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Analysis of genetic data opens up many opportunities for medical and scientific advances. The use of phenotypic information and polygenic risk scores to analyze genetic data is widespread. Most work on genetic privacy focuses on basic genetic data such as SNP values and specific genotypes. In this paper, we introduce a novel methodology to quantify and prevent privacy risks by focusing on polygenic scores and phenotypic information. Our methodology is based on the tool-supported privacy risk analysis method Privug. We demonstrate the use of Privug to assess privacy risks posed by disclosing a polygenic trait score for bitter taste receptors, encoded by TAS2R38 and TAS2R16, to a person's privacy in regards to their ethnicity. We provide an extensive privacy risks analysis of different programs for genetic data disclosure: taster phenotype, tasting polygenic score, and a polygenic score distorted with noise. Finally, we discuss the privacy/utility trade-offs of the polygenic score.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Pardo, Raúl","Rafnsson, Willard","Steinhorn, Gregor","Lavrov, Denis","Lumley, Thomas","Probst, Christian","Ziedins, Ilze","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695280"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"country":["New Zealand"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","The University of Auckland","UNITEC Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Genetic Data Analysis","Genetic Privacy","Phenotypic Information","Polygenic risk scores","Privacy Risk Analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"privacy with good taste a case study in quantifying privacy risks in genetic scores","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/license.html","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2208.12497.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-695280","ids":["itu-b0eeda5b-b02a-4c79-b017-ce7acb40311a"],"keyword":["Genetic Data Analysis","Genetic Privacy","Phenotypic Information","Polygenic Risk Scores","Privacy Risk Analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AD3A5F4CF85C992F04BF692FB7C3BE22"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/license.html","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2208.12497.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nz","key":"unitec institute of technology","loc":["New Zealand","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"UNITEC Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nz","key":"the university of auckland","loc":["New Zealand","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"The University of Auckland","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Raúl","key":"pardopau","last":"Pardo","locid":"d05daa00-c3d6-4a89-ba14-cfd1847fb0cc","name":"Pardo, Raúl","orcid":"0000-0003-0003-7295","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Willard","key":"rafnssonpau","last":"Rafnsson","locid":"9cf737ee-bd9a-4f7e-b865-b6ff6ed01fde","name":"Rafnsson, Willard","orcid":"0000-0003-1482-3094","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Gregor","key":"steinhornpau","last":"Steinhorn","name":"Steinhorn, Gregor","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Denis","key":"lavrovpau","last":"Lavrov","name":"Lavrov, Denis","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"lumleypau","last":"Lumley","name":"Lumley, Thomas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"probstpau","last":"Probst","name":"Probst, Christian","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ilze","key":"ziedinspau","last":"Ziedins","name":"Ziedins, Ilze","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9783031257346"],"isbn":["9783031257339"],"pages":"1-16","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Privacy with Good Taste: A Case Study in Quantifying Privacy Risks in Genetic Scores","volume":"13619"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85149861159"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b0eeda5b-b02a-4c79-b017-ce7acb40311a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Privacy with Good Taste: A Case Study in Quantifying Privacy Risks in Genetic Scores","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-695280","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
