,"url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.31-038276","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Anonymization is viewed as a solution to over-exposure of personal information in a data-driven society. Yet how organizations apply anonymization techniques to data for regulatory, ethical or commercial reasons remains underexplored. We investigate how such measures are applied in organizations, asking whether anonymization practices are used, what approaches are considered practical and adequate, and how decisions are made to protect the privacy of data subjects while preserving analytical value. Our findings demonstrate that anonymization is applied to data far less pervasively than expected. Organizations that do employ anonymization often view their practices as sensitive and resort to anonymity by obscurity alongside technical means. Rather than being a purely technical question of applying the right algorithms, anonymization in practice is a complex socio-technical process that relies on multi-stakeholder collaborations. Organizational decision-making about appropriate approaches and the management of responsibility can result in workarounds necessary to negotiate the technical complexit","author_count":3,"contributors":["Hargitai, Viktor","Shklovski, Irina","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384056"],"event":{"acronym":"CSCW","title":"ACM Conference on Computer Supported Cooperative Work"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Anonymization"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"going beyond obscurity organizational approaches to data anonymization","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83854564/Going_Beyond_Obscurity.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384056","identifier":[{"id":"85066421720","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-be45220b-23ca-4838-9fac-9ebfa9a1de98"],"keyword":["anonymization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B665387A8246A5FCAF034E75EC7CCC95"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83854564/Going_Beyond_Obscurity.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Viktor","key":"hargitaipau","last":"Hargitai","name":"Hargitai, Viktor","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Irina","key":"shklovskipau","last":"Shklovski","name":"Shklovski, Irina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3274335","issn":["25730142"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"Proceedings of the ACM on Human-Computer Interaction - CSCW","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the ACM on Human-Computer Interaction - CSCW","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85066421720"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-be45220b-23ca-4838-9fac-9ebfa9a1de98"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Going Beyond Obscurity: Organizational Approaches to Data Anonymization","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384056","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In Model-Driven Software Development, models are automatically processed to support the creation, build, and execution of systems. A large variety of dedicated model-transformation languages exists, promising to efficiently realize the automated processing of models. To investigate the actual benefit of using such specialized languages, we performed a large-scale controlled experiment in which over 78 subjects solve 231 individual tasks using three languages. The experiment sheds light on commonalities and differences between model transformation languages (ATL, QVT-O) and on benefits of using them in common development tasks (comprehension, change, and creation) against a modern general-purpose language (Xtend). Our results show no statistically significant benefit of using a dedicated transformation language over a modern general-purpose language. However, we were able to identify several aspects of transformation programming where domain-specific transformation languages do appear to help, including copying objects, context identification, and conditioning the computation on types.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Hebig, Regina","Berger, Thorsten","Seidl, Christoph","Kook Pedersen, John","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381608"],"event":{"acronym":"ESEC/FSE","title":"ACM Joint European Software Engineering Conference and Symposium on the Foundations of Software Engineering (ESEC/FSE)"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chalmers University of Technology","Technical University of Braunschweig","University of Gothenburg"],"keyword":["ATL","Change Tasks","Comprehension Tasks","Copying Objects","Domain specific languages","General Purpose Languages","Model Driven Software Development","Model Transformation Languages","QVT O","Transformation Programming"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"model transformation languages under a magnifying glass a controlled experiment with xtend atl and qvt","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83700789/2018_fse_model_trafos_regina_thorsten_christoph.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381608","identifier":[{"id":"85058341895","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-168e395e-91c5-4d37-8276-9477539eab85"],"keyword":["ATL","Change Tasks","Comprehension Tasks","Copying Objects","Domain-Specific Languages","General-Purpose Languages","Model Transformation Languages","Model-Driven Software Development","QVT-O","Transformation Programming"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-929F2A7298F7621E91176A11CA49B87F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83700789/2018_fse_model_trafos_regina_thorsten_christoph.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"chalmers university of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Chalmers University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"university of gothenburg","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Gothenburg","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"technical university of braunschweig","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Technical University of Braunschweig","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Software Engineering, Software Quality Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Regina","key":"hebigpau","last":"Hebig","name":"Hebig, Regina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thorsten","key":"bergerpau","last":"Berger","name":"Berger, Thorsten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Christoph","key":"seidlpau","last":"Seidl","name":"Seidl, Christoph","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"John","key":"kookpedersenpau","last":"Kook Pedersen","name":"Kook Pedersen, John","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3236024.3236046","isbn":["9781450355735"],"pages":"445-455","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2018 ACM Joint Meeting on European Software Engineering Conference and Symposium on the Foundations of Software Engineering, ESEC/SIGSOFT FSE 2018, Lake Buena Vista, FL, USA, November 04-09, 2018"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85058341895"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-168e395e-91c5-4d37-8276-9477539eab85"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Model transformation languages under a magnifying glass: a controlled experiment with Xtend, ATL, and QVT","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381608","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
