corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2997364.2997382","isbn":["9781450344470"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 9th ACM SIGPLAN International Conference on Software Language Engineering"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85006790383"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-1ea79a5b-31c2-437e-baa7-d4a300e1c496"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Symbolic Execution of High-Level Transformations","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381725","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Software projects embrace variability to increase adaptability and to lower cost; however, others blame variability for increasing complexity and making reasoning about programs more difficult. We carry out a controlled experiment to quantify the impact of variability on debugging of preprocessor-based programs. We measure speed and precision for bug finding tasks defined at three different degrees of variability on several subject programs derived from real systems. The results show that the speed of bug finding decreases linearly with the number of features, while effectiveness of finding bugs is relatively independent of the degree of variability. Still, identifying the set of configurations in which the bug manifests itself is difficult already for a low number of features. Surprisingly, identifying the exact set of affected configurations appears to be harder than finding the bug in the first place. The difficulty in reasoning about several configurations is a likely reason why the variability bugs are actually introduced in configurable programs. We hope that the detailed findings presented here will inspire the creation of programmer support tools addressing the challenges faced by developers when reasoning about configurations, contributing to more effective debugging and, ultimately, fewer bugs in highly-configurable systems.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Melo, Jean","Brabrand, Claus","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381836"],"event":{"acronym":"ICSE","title":"International Conference on Software Engineering"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bug finding strategies","Configuration complexity","Debugging performance","Preprocessor based programs","Variability Management"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how does the degree of variability affect bug finding","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://itu.dk/people/jeam/variability-experiment/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381836","identifier":[{"id":"84971432042","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-25affa62-4c95-4325-9b07-8173a2733515"],"keyword":["Bug finding strategies","Configuration complexity","Debugging performance","Preprocessor-based programs","Variability management"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9E89416AFFEF2325836AB2BC6B140C35"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jean","key":"melopau","last":"Melo","name":"Melo, Jean","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","locid":"47a94200-3abe-4354-b5e3-c8ef6f1ba1f2","name":"Brabrand, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-5093-5806","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2884781.2884831","isbn":["9781450339001"],"pages":"679-690","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ICSE '16 Proceedings of the 38th International Conference on Software Engineering"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84971432042"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-25affa62-4c95-4325-9b07-8173a2733515"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"How Does the Degree of Variability Affect Bug-Finding?","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381836","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"The quantification of information leakage provides a quantitative evaluation of the security of a system. We propose the usage of Markovian processes to model deterministic and probabilistic systems. By using a methodology generalizing the lattice of information approach we model refined attackers capable to observe the internal behavior of the system, and quantify the information leakage of such systems. We also use our method to obtain an algorithm for the computation of channel capacity from our Markovian models. Finally, we show how to use the method to analyze timed and non-timed attacks on the Onion Routing protocol.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Biondi, Fabrizio","Legay, Axel","Malacaria, Pasquale","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383757"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["France","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Queen Mary University of London","The French National Institute for Computer Science (INRIA)"],"keyword":["Channel capacity","Information leakage","Markov chain","Markov decision process","Model checking","Probabilistic system","Quantitative information flow"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quantifying information leakage of randomized protocols","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81828159/tcs15.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-383757","identifier":[{"id":"84939257285","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ab564829-be8d-430e-9ba6-143e0e99e00b"],"keyword":["Channel capacity","Information leakage","Markov chain","Markov decision process","Model checking","Probabilistic system","Quantitative information flow"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-63FCF46CBAB25997B20978932289DCD1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81828159/tcs15.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fr","key":"the french national institute for computer science","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"The French National Institute for Computer Science (INRIA)","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"queen mary university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Queen Mary University of London","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabrizio","key":"biondipau","last":"Biondi","name":"Biondi, Fabrizio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Axel","key":"legaypau","last":"Legay","name":"Legay, Axel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Pasquale","key":"malacariapau","last":"Malacaria","name":"Malacaria, Pasquale","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.tcs.2015.07.034","issn":["03043975"],"journal":"Theoretical Computer Science","pages":"62-87","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Theoretical Computer Science","volum