{"abstract":"A specification theory combines notions of specifications and implementations with a satisfaction relation, a refinement relation, and a set of operators supporting stepwise design. We develop a specification framework for real-time systems using Timed I/O Automata as the specification formalism, with the semantics expressed in terms of Timed I/O Transition Systems. We provide constructs for refinement, consistency checking, logical and structural composition, and quotient of specifications-all indispensable ingredients of a compositional design methodology. The theory is implemented in the new tool Ecdar. We present symbolic versions of the algorithms used in Ecdar, and demonstrate the use of the tool using a small case study in compositional verification.","author_count":6,"contributors":["David, Alexandre","Larsen, Kim Guldstrand","Legay, A.","Nyman, Ulrik","Traonouez, L.-M.","Wasowski, A."],"cuid":["S02-091.11-003897"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia","France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","INRIA/IRISA, Rennes Cedex, France","The French National Institute for Computer Science (INRIA)"],"keyword":["Compositional verification","Real time systems","Stepwise refinement","Timed I O automata"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"real time specifications","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/87317469/Real_timeSpecificationsSTTT2013.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-091.11-003897","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000355681700002","type":"wos"},{"id":"84921999725","type":"scopus"