{"abstract":"Introducing automated formal methods for large industrial real-time systems is an important research challenge. We propose timed process automata (TPA) for modeling and analysis of time-critical systems which can be open, hierarchical, and dynamic. The model offers two essential features for large industrial systems: (i) compositional modeling with reusable designs for different contexts, and (ii) an automated state-space reduction technique. Timed process automata model dynamic networks of continuous-time communicating control processes which can activate other processes. We show how to automatically establish safety and reachability properties of TPA by reduction to solving timed games. To mitigate the state-space explosion problem, an automated state-space reduction technique using compositional reasoning and aggressive abstractions is also proposed.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Bin Waez, Md Tawhid","Wasowski, Andrzej","Dingel, Juergen","Rudie, Karen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383169"],"event":{"acronym":"VMCAI","title":"International Conference on Verification, Model Checking, and Abstract Interpretation"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Queen’s University"],"keyword":["Automated formal methods","Compositional modeling","State space reduction","Timed games","Timed process automata"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a model for industrial real time systems","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81828612/FTPA.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383169","identifier":[{"id":"84917707007","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-8168b182-6edc-4025-93c2-b40aa75482c2"],"keyword":["Automated formal methods","Compositional modeling","State-space reduction","Timed games","Timed process automata"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E17BD2A54CD62C95A22A837D835B3DA2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81828612/FTPA.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ca","key":"queen s university","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Queen’s University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Md Tawhid","key":"binwaezpau","last":"Bin Waez","name":"Bin Waez, Md Tawhid","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Juergen","key":"dingelpau","last":"Dingel","name":"Dingel, Juergen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen","key":"rudiepau","last":"Rudie","name":"Rudie, Karen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Deepak","key":"dsouzapedh","last":"D'Souza","name":"D'Souza, Deepak","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Akash","key":"lalpedh","last":"Lal","name":"Lal, Akash","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kim","key":"guldstrandlarsenpedh","last":"Guldstrand Larsen","name":"Guldstrand Larsen, Kim","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-662-46081-8_9","isbn":["9783662460801"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"153-171","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"16th International Conference, VMCAI 2015, Mumbai, India, January 12-14, 2015. Proceedings.","title":"Verification, Model Checking, and Abstract Interpretation","volume":"8931"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84917707007"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-8168b182-6edc-4025-93c2-b40aa75482c2"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Model for Industrial Real-Time Systems","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383169","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Many software systems are variational: they can be configured to meet diverse sets of requirements. Variability is found in both communication protocols and discrete controllers of embedded systems. In these areas, model checking is an important verification technique. For variational models (systems with variability), specialized family-based model checking algorithms allow efficient verification of multiple variants, simultaneously. These algorithms scale much better than ``brute force'' verification of individual systems, one-by-one. Nevertheless, they can deal with only very small variational models. We address two key problems of family-based model checking. First, we improve scalability by introducing abstractions that simplify variability. Second, we reduce the burden of maintaining specialized family-based model checkers, by showing how the presented variability abstractions can be used to model-check variational models using the standard version of (single system) SPIN. The abstractions are first defined as Galois connections on semantic domains. We then show how to translate them into syntactic source-to-source transformations on variational models. This allows the use of SPIN with all its accumulated optimizations for efficient verification of variational models without any knowledge about variability. We demonstrate the practicality of this method on several examples using both the SNIP (family based) and SPIN (single system) model checkers.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Dimovski, Aleksandar","Al-Sibahi, Ahmad Salim","Brabrand, Claus","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384700"],"event":{"acronym":"SPIN","end":"2015-08-26","place":"Stellenbosch, za","start":"2015-08-24","title":"22nd International SPIN Symposium on Model Checking of Software","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Family Based Abstract Model Checking","Model Checkers","Variability Abstractions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"family based model checking without a family based model checker","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81821925/dimovski_spin15.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384700","identifier":[{"id":"84945924168","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-e8d276b3-fd2b-427d-8079-e9ec01c7cf7a"],"keyword":["Family-Based Abstract Model Checking","Model Checkers","Variability Abstractions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-73FC14EC791DC2298ABB574AC8C3AA2B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81821925/dimovski_spin15.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Aleksandar","key":"dimovskipau","last":"Dimovski","name":"Dimovski, Aleksandar","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ahmad Salim","key":"alsibahipau","last":"Al-Sibahi","name":"Al-Sibahi, Ahmad Salim","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","locid":"47a94200-3abe-4354-b5e3-c8ef6f1ba1f2","name":"Brabrand, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-5093-5806","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"B.","key":"fischerpedh","last":"Fischer","name":"Fischer, B.","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"J.","key":"geldenhuyspedh","last":"Geldenhuys","name":"Geldenhuys, J.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-23404-5_18","isbn":["9783319234038"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"282-299","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"22nd International Symposium, SPIN 2015, Stellenbosch, South Africa, August 24-26, 2015, Proceedings","title":"Model Checking Software","volume":"9232"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84945924168"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-e8d276b3-fd2b-427d-8079-e9ec01c7cf7a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Family-Based Model Checking Without a Family-Based Model Checker","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384700","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Variant-rich software systems offer a large degree of customization, allowing users to configure the target system according to their preferences and needs. Facing high degrees of variability, these systems often employ variability models to explicitly capture user-configurable features (e.g., systems options) and the constraints they impose. The explicit representation of features allows them to be referenced in different variation points across different artifacts, enabling the latter to vary according to specific feature selections. In such settings, the evolution of variability models interplays with the evolution of related artifacts, requiring the two to evolve together, or coevolve. Interestingly, little is known about how such coevolution occurs in real-world systems, as existing research has focused mostly on variability evolution as it happens in variability models only. Furthermore, existing techniques supporting variability evolution are usually validated with randomly-generated variability models or evolution scenarios that do not stem from practice. As the community lacks a deep understanding of how variability evolution occurs in real-world systems and how it relates to the evolution of different kinds of software artifacts, it is not surprising that industry reports existing tools and solutions ineffective, as they do not handle the complexity found in practice. Attempting to mitigate this overall lack of knowledge and to support tool builders with insights on how variability models coevolve with other artifact types, we study a large and complex real-world variant-rich software system: the Linux kernel. Specifically, we extract variability-coevolution patterns capturing changes in the variability model of the Linux kernel with subsequent changes in Makefiles and C source code. From the analysis of the patterns, we report on findings concerning evolution principles found in the kernel, and we reveal deficiencies in existing tools and theory when handling changes captured by our patterns.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Passos, Leonardo","Teixeira, Leopoldo","Dinztner, Nicolas","Apel, Sven","Wasowski, Andrzej","Czarnecki, Krzysztof","Borba, Paulo","Guo, Jianmei"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-384340"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","America, South","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Brazil","Canada","Germany","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Delft University of Technology","Federal University of Pernambuco","University of Passau","University of Waterloo"],"keyword":["Evolution","Linux","Patterns","Software product lines","Variability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"coevolution of variability models and related software artifacts","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81832580/Coevolution_of_variability_models_and_related_software_artifacts.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-384340","identifier":[{"id":"84928713229","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-d169c694-0039-4ffd-a5c9-2b39dc7df97c"],"keyword":["Evolution","Linux","Patterns","Software Product Lines","Variability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E8144DCFFCEA341852179FB3DC249A04"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/81832580/Coevolution_of_variability_models_and_related_software_artifacts.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ca","key":"university of waterloo","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],