{"abstract":"Feature-sensitive verification pursues effective analysis of the exponentially many variants of a program family. However, researchers lack examples of concrete bugs induced by variability, occurring in real large-scale systems. Such a collection of bugs is a requirement for goal-oriented research, serving to evaluate tool implementations of feature-sensitive analyses by testing them on real bugs. We present a qualitative study of 42 variability bugs collected from bug-fixing commits to the Linux kernel repository. We analyze each of the bugs, and record the results in a database. In addition, we provide self-contained simplified C99 versions of the bugs, facilitating understanding and tool evaluation. Our study provides insights into the nature and occurrence of variability bugs in a large C software system, and shows in what ways variability affects and increases the complexity of software bugs.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Abal, Iago","Brabrand, Claus","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382385"],"event":{"acronym":"ASE","end":"2014-09-19","place":"Västerås, se","start":"2014-09-15","title":"IEEE/ACM International Conference on Automated Software Engineering","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bugs","Feature interactions","Linux","Software Variability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000042 variability bugs in the linux kernel a qualitative study","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84908635167","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382385","identifier":[{"id":"84908635167","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4aea84e9-050f-4dfb-a0e8-25f12437ee00"],"keyword":["Bugs","Feature interactions","Linux","Software Variability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-13347C8E6B68CA181E0B239DC5B8CCDF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Iago","key":"abalpau","last":"Abal","name":"Abal, Iago","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","locid":"47a94200-3abe-4354-b5e3-c8ef6f1ba1f2","name":"Brabrand, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-5093-5806","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781450330138"],"pages":"421-432","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"ASE '14 Proceedings of the 29th ACM/IEEE international conference on Automated software engineering"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4aea84e9-050f-4dfb-a0e8-25f12437ee00"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"42 Variability Bugs in the Linux Kernel : A Qualitative Study","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382385","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"A recent line of work lifts particular verification and analysis methods to Software Product Lines (SPL). In an effort to generalize such case-by-case approaches, we develop a systematic methodology for lifting program analyses to SPLs using abstract interpretation. Abstract interpretation is a classical framework for deriving static analyses in a compositional, step-by-step manner. We show how to take an analysis expressed as an abstract interpretation and lift each of the abstract interpretation steps to a family of programs. This includes schemes for how to lift domain types, and combinators for lifting analyses and Galois connections. We prove that for analyses developed using our method, the soundness of lifting follows by construction. Finally, we discuss approximating variability in an analysis and we derive variational data-flow equations for an example analysis, a constant propagation analysis for a simple imperative language.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Midtgaard, Jan","Brabrand, Claus","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S02-084.04-027177"],"event":{"end":"2014-04-25","place":"Lugano, ch","start":"2014-04-22","title":"International Conference on Modularity","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Abstract Interpretation","Software product lines","Static analysis","Verification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"systematic derivation of static analyses for software product lines","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/74512903/TR_2014_170.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-084.04-027177","identifier":[{"id":"84900021591","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c843ab67-bc94-4445-bd74-f580b1345948","itu-a492a6d7-e0c3-44cf-9c82-fc664cb54812"],"keyword":["Abstract Interpretation","Software product lines","Static Analysis","verification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-209CDAA8D07A082527E8A87342D9E93C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dl.acm.org/citation.cfm?id=2577091","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/74512903/TR_2014_170.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/2577080.2577091","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"midtgaardpau","last":"Midtgaard","locid":"bc81b2f8-5fda-47b6-b465-49732e3919a5","name":"Midtgaard, Jan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","locid":"47a94200-3abe-4354-b5e3-c8ef6f1ba1f2","name":"Brabrand, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-5093-5806","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Walter","key":"binderpedh","last":"Binder","name":"Binder, Walter","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2577080.2577091","edition":"TR-2014-170","eisbn":["9788779493087"],"isbn":["9781450327725"],"issn":["16006100"],"issue":"TR-2014-170","pages":"181-192","place":"Copenhagen","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"IT University Technical Report Series","status":"p","title":"MODULARITY '14 Proceedings of the 13th international conference on Modularity"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84900021591"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c843ab67-bc94-4445-bd74-f580b1345948","itu-a492a6d7-e0c3-44cf-9c82-fc664cb54812"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Systematic Derivation of Static Analyses for Software Product Lines","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-084.04-027177","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Modal specification is a well-known formalism used as an abstraction theory for tran- sition systems. Modal specifications are transition systems equipped with two types of transitions: must-transitions that are mandatory to any implementation, and may- transitions that are optional. The duality of transitions allows for developing a unique approach for both logical and structural compositions, and eases the step-wise refine- ment process for building implementations. We propose Modal Specifications with Data (MSDs), the first modal specification theory with explicit representation of data. Our new theory includes the most commonly seen ingredients of a specification the- ory; that is parallel composition, conjunction and quotient. As MSDs are by nature potentially infinite-state systems, we propose symbolic representations based on effec- tive predicates. Our theory serves as a new abstraction-based formalism for transition systems with data.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Bauer, Sebastian S.","Larsen, Kim Guldstrand","Legay, Axel","Nyman, Ulrik","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S02-087.88-007153"],"event":{"end":"2011-11-16","place":"Oslo, no","start":"2011-11-14","title":"8th International Workshop, FACS 2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","INRIA/IRISA, Rennes Cedex","Institut für Informatik, Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","The French National Institute for Computer Science (INRIA)"],"keyword":["Data abstraction","Interfaces","Modal specifications with data","Modal transition systems","Specifications"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a modal specification theory for components with data","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/87321953/ownSCP2013.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-087.88-007153","identifier":[{"id":"84894584009","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000333945900006","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-93c73daa-66b4-4701-ab30-8e9d967daf89","itu-c31c0a4e-62a9-4ca4-900d-3e7b0e4a83f4"],"keyword":["Data abstraction","Interfaces","Modal Transition Systems, Specifications, Interfaces, Data Abstraction, Modal Specifications with Data","Modal specifications with data","Modal transition systems","Specifications"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B3280C678FC2979C709E7CFE93F91F09"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/87321953/ownSCP2013.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.scico.2013.06.003","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"institut für informatik ludwig maximilians universität münchen","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Institut für Informatik, Ludwig-Maximilians-Universität München","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"ludwig maximilian university of munich","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Depa