{"abstract":"Variability modeling, and in particular feature modeling, is a central element of model-driven software product line architectures. Such architectures often emerge from legacy code, but, creating feature models from large, legacy systems is a long and arduous task. We describe three synthesis scenarios that can benefit from the algorithms in this paper.","author_count":5,"contributors":["She, Steven","Ryssel, Uwe","Andersen, Nele","Wasowski, Andrzej","Czarnecki, Krzysztof"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383689"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Canada","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","TU Dresden","University of Waterloo"],"keyword":["Feature models","Software product lines","Variability models"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"efficient synthesis of feature models","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84901604748","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383689","identifier":[{"id":"84901604748","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a5e86dcc-477c-4d8a-8dfd-f20e9df921db"],"keyword":["Feature models","Software product lines","Variability models"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C54D1845C0B06DB71301ACAF8AFFC3EE"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ca","key":"university of waterloo","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Waterloo","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"tu dresden","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"TU Dresden","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steven","key":"shepau","last":"She","name":"She, Steven","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Uwe","key":"rysselpau","last":"Ryssel","name":"Ryssel, Uwe","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Nele","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Nele","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Krzysztof","key":"czarneckipau","last":"Czarnecki","name":"Czarnecki, Krzysztof","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09505849","18736025"],"issn_org":["09505849"],"issue":"9","journal":"Information and Software Technology","pages":"1122-1143","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Information and Software Technology","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84901604748"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a5e86dcc-477c-4d8a-8dfd-f20e9df921db"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Efficient synthesis of feature models","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383689","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The channel capacity of a deterministic system with confidential data is an upper bound on the amount of bits of data an attacker can learn from the system. We encode all possible attacks to a system using a probabilistic specification, an Interval Markov Chain. Then the channel capacity computation reduces to finding a model of a specification with highest entropy. Entropy maximization for probabilistic process specifications has not been studied before, even though it is well known in Bayesian inference for discrete distributions. We give a characterization of global entropy of a process as a reward function, a polynomial algorithm to verify the existence of a system maximizing entropy among those respecting a specification, a procedure for the maximization of reward functions over Interval Markov Chains and its application to synthesize an implementation maximizing entropy. We show how to use Interval Markov Chains to model abstractions of deterministic systems with confidential data, and use the above results to compute their channel capacity. These results are a foundation for ongoing work on computing channel capacity for abstractions of programs derived from code. © 2014 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Biondi, Fabrizio","Legay, Axel","Nielsen, Bo Friis","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S02-085.41-032744"],"event":{"acronym":"NWPT","end":"2012-11-02","place":"Bergen, no","start":"2012-10-31","title":"24th Nordic Workshop on Programming Theory (NWPT 2012)","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","French National Institute for Computer Science and Applied Mathematics","The French National Institute for Computer Science (INRIA)"],"keyword":["Channel capacity","Confidential Data","Deterministic Systems","Entropy Maximization","Interval Markov Chains"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"maximizing entropy over markov processes","src":["dtu","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/37299633/main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-085.41-032744","identifier":[{"id":"84938680276","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-073485a8-c4f6-4cdd-afc7-8a3d38ff9c9e","itu-e8142147-f793-4aa6-9f24-d120f21c489b"],"keyword":["Channel Capacity","Confidential Data","Deterministic Systems","Entropy Maximization","Interval Markov Chains"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-9150173E2E0C5FE9C2E2D57E2E30E394"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jlamp.2014.05.001","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/37299633/main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"french national institute for computer science and applied mathematics","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"French National Institute for Computer Science and Applied Mathematics","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"fr","key":"the french national institute for computer science","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"The French National Institute for Computer Science (INRIA)","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Statistics and Data Analysis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabrizio","key":"biondipau","last":"Biondi","name":"Biondi, Fabrizio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Axel","key":"legaypau","last":"Legay","name":"Legay, Axel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bo Friis","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"364b98b5-e608-4186-a566-62fa91a37d59","name":"Nielsen, Bo Friis","orcid":"0000-0001-9146-9733","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jlamp.2014.05.001","issn":["23522208","23522216"],"issn_org":["23522208"],"issue":"5-6","journal":"Journal of Logic and Algebraic Programming","pages":"384-399","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Logic and Algebraic Programming","volume":"83"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84938680276"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-073485a8-c4f6-4cdd-afc7-8a3d38ff9c9e","itu-e8142147-f793-4aa6-9f24-d120f21c489b"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Maximizing Entropy over Markov Processes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-085.41-032744","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Feature-sensitive verification is a recent field that pursues the effective analysis of the exponential number of variants of a program family. Today researchers lack examples of concrete bugs induced by variability, and occurring in real large-scale software. Such a collection of bugs is a requirement for goal-oriented research, serving to evaluate tool implementations of feature-sensitive analyses by testing them on real bugs. We present a qualitative study of 40 variability bugs collected from bug-fixing commits to the Linux kernel repository. We investigate each of the 40 bugs, recording the outcome of our analysis into a database. In addition, we provide self-contained simplified C99 versions of the bugs, facilitating understanding and tool evaluation. Our study provides insights about the nature and occurrence of variability bugs in a large C software system, and shows in what ways variability affects and increases the complexity of software bugs.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Abal Rivas, Iago","Brabrand, Claus","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381478"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bug Analysis","Feature Sensitive Verification","Linux kernel","Software Complexity","Variability Bugs"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000040 variability bugs in the linux kernel a qualitative study","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/74775263/ITU_TR_2014_180.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-381478","ids":["itu-0e49901a-4f89-4a2e-a2bd-be21da8efe97"],"keyword":["Bug Analysis","Feature-Sensitive Verification","Linux Kernel","Software Complexity","Variability Bugs"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-721811C6D70301D37671B4EE30CB2591"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/74775263/ITU_TR_2014_180.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Iago","key":"abalrivaspau","last":"Abal Rivas","name":"Abal Rivas, Iago","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"brabrandpau","last":"Brabrand","locid":"47a94200-3abe-4354-b5e3-c8ef6f1ba1f2","name":"Brabrand, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-5093-5806","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16006100"],"issue":"TR-2014-180","pages":"20","place":"Copenhagen","publisher":"IT-Universitetet i København","repno":"IT University Technical Report Series, TR-2014-180","series":"IT University Technical Report Series","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0e49901a-4f89-4a2e-a2bd-be21da8efe97"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"40 Variability Bugs in the Linux Kernel : A Qualitative Study","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381478","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
