{"abstract":"The quantification of information leakage provides a quantitative evaluation of the security of a system. We propose the usage of Markovian processes to model and analyze the information leakage of deterministic and probabilistic systems. We show that this method generalizes the lattice of information approach and is a natural framework for modeling refined attackers capable to observe the internal behavior of the system. We also use our method to obtain an algorithm for the computation of channel capacity from our Markovian models. Finally, we show how to use the method to analyze timed and non-timed attacks on the Onion Routing protocol.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Biondi, Fabrizio","Wasowski, Andrzej","Legay, Axel","Malacaria, Pasquale"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381875"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["France","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Queen Mary University of London","The French National Institute for Computer Science (INRIA)"],"keyword":["Channel capacity","Information leakage","Markov chain","Markov decision process","Onion routing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quantifying information leakage of randomized protocols","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/37299572/main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381875","identifier":[{"id":"84893791384","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-28a4c597-eed1-4ca9-bfe6-ee22291e55bc"],"keyword":["Channel capacity","Information leakage","Markov Decision Process","Markov chain","Onion routing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C18D146AB8EA5AACA05D4E17B08F626A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/37299572/main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"the french national institute for computer science","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"The French National Institute for Computer Science (INRIA)","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"queen mary university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Queen Mary University of London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabrizio","key":"biondipau","last":"Biondi","name":"Biondi, Fabrizio","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Axel","key":"legaypau","last":"Legay","name":"Legay, Axel","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Pasquale","key":"malacariapau","last":"Malacaria","name":"Malacaria, Pasquale","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["03029743","16113349"],"issn_org":["03029743"],"journal":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","pages":"68-87","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"7737"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84893791384"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-28a4c597-eed1-4ca9-bfe6-ee22291e55bc"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Quantifying Information Leakage of Randomized Protocols","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381875","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Variability models represent the common and variable features of products in a product line. Since the introduction of FODA in 1990, several variability modeling languages have been proposed in academia and industry, followed by hundreds of research papers on variability models and modeling. However, little is known about the practical use of such languages. We study the constructs, semantics, usage, and associated tools of two variability modeling languages, Kconfig and CDL, which are independently developed outside academia and used in large and significant software projects. We analyze 128 variability models found in 12 open--source projects using these languages. Our study 1) supports variability modeling research with empirical data on the real-world use of its flagship concepts. However, we 2) also provide requirements for concepts and mechanisms that are not commonly considered in academic techniques, and 3) challenge assumptions about size and complexity of variability models made in academic papers. These results are of interest to researchers working on variability modeling and analysis techniques and to designers of tools, such as feature dependency checkers and interactive product configurators.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Berger, Thorsten","She, Steven","Lotufo, Rafael","Wasowski, Andrzej","Czarnecki, Krzysztof"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383148"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Waterloo"],"keyword":["Configuration","Empirical Software Engineering","Feature Modeling","Open source","Software product lines","Variability Modeling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a study of variability models and languages in the systems software domain","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/TSE.2013.34","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383148","identifier":[{"id":"84890065386","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-807e4572-623e-4743-8154-12a36bb30e21"],"keyword":["Empirical software engineering","configuration","feature modeling","open source","software product lines","variability modeling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E1C9F88E60ACC3EA866D8ABF2A6D8175"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/TSE.2013.34","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["The Department, Software & Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"university of waterloo","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Waterloo","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thorsten","key":"bergerpau","last":"Berger","name":"Berger, Thorsten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Steven","key":"shepau","last":"She","name":"She, Steven","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rafael","key":"lotufopau","last":"Lotufo","name":"Lotufo, Rafael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","correspon