{"abstract":"Probabilistic Automata (PAs) are a widely-recognized mathematical framework for the specification and analysis of systems with non-deterministic and stochastic behaviors. This paper proposes Abstract Probabilistic Automata (APAs), that is a novel abstraction model for PAs. In APAs uncertainty of the non-deterministic choices is modeled by may/must modalities on transitions while uncertainty of the stochastic behavior is expressed by (underspecified) stochastic constraints. We have developed a complete abstraction theory for PAs, and also propose the first specification theory for them. Our theory supports both satisfaction and refinement operators, together with classical stepwise design operators. In addition, we study the link between specification theories and abstraction in avoiding the state-space explosion problem.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Delahaye, B.","Katoen, Joost Pieter","Larsen, Kim Guldstrand","Legay, Axel","Pedersen, Mikkel L.","Sher, Falak","Wa̧sowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S02-096.25-007897"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Legay, Axel"],"country":["France","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","INRIA/IRISA","RWTH Aachen University","The French National Institute for Computer Science (INRIA)"],"keyword":["Abstraction","Compositional reasoning","Interface automata","Probabilistic Automata","Specification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"abstract probabilistic automata","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ic.2013.10.002","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-096.25-007897","identifier":[{"id":"000328524600005","type":"wos"},{"id":"84886676068","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-a37ab485-f3df-4a23-863c-f9c4e48b37e4","itu-6c95463f-3f9d-4433-b1b8-32dee649f2b0"],"keyword":["Abstraction","Compositional reasoning","Interface automata","Probabilistic Automata","Specification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-51612974FA54B4D964E4A3746CFA3367"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=84886676068&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ic.2013.10.002","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"the french national institute for computer science","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"The French National Institute for Computer Science (INRIA)","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"rwth aachen university","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"RWTH Aachen University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fr","key":"inria irisa","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"INRIA/IRISA","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Co