{"abstract":"We present a specification theory for timed systems implemented in the Ecdar tool. We illustrate the operations of the specification theory on a running example, showing the models and verification checks. To demonstrate the power of the compositional verification, we perform an in depth case study of a leader election protocol; Modeling it in Ecdar as Timed input/output automata Specifications and performing both monolithic and compositional verification of two interesting properties on it. We compare the execution time of the compositional to the classical verification showing a huge difference in favor of compositional verification.","author_count":8,"contributors":["David, Alexandre","Larsen, Kim Guldstrand","Møller, Mikael Harkjær","Nyman, Ulrik","Ravn, Anders Peter","Skou, Arne","Legay, Axel","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-007350"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Compositional verification","Leader election protocol","Real time systems","Timed input output automata"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"compositional verification of real time systems using ecdar","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/65653882/ownSTTT2012.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-100.00-007350","identifier":[{"id":"84867404484","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-9794c783-97d2-4fe3-acaa-7d3de1b2e67d","itu-0fed01f2-9af7-4c3c-82a2-49880f53327a"],"keyword":["Compositional verification","Leader election protocol","Real-time systems","Timed input/output automata"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Loca