corresponding":null,"first":"Øystein","key":"haugenpau","last":"Haugen","name":"Haugen, Øystein","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Krzysztof","key":"czarneckipau","last":"Czarnecki","name":"Czarnecki, Krzysztof","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2364412.2364462","isbn":["9781450310956"],"pages":"266-267","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"16th International Software Product Line Conference, SPLC'12, Salvador, Brazil - September 2-7, 2012, Volume 2","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84867477691"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-d979f2ca-d21f-45a2-bc7e-1a1cdd78e263"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"CVL: common variability language","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-384469","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"This paper studies compositional reasoning theories for stochastic systems. A specification theory combines notions of specification and implementation with satisfaction and refinement relations, and a set of operators that together support stepwise design. One of the first behavioral specification theories introduced for stochastic systems is the one of Interval Markov Chains (IMCs), which are Markov Chains whose probability distributions are replaced by a conjunction of intervals. In this paper, we show that IMCs are not closed under conjunction, which gives a formal proof of a conjecture made in several recent works. In order to leverage this problem, we suggested to work with Constraint Markov Chains (CMCs) that is another specification theory where intervals are replaced with general constraints. Contrary to IMCs, one can show that CMCs enjoy the closure properties of a specification theory. In addition, we propose aggressive abstraction procedures for CMCs. Such abstractions can be used either to combat the state-space explosion problem, or to simplify complex constraints. In particular, one can show that, under some assumptions, the behavior of any CMC can be abstracted by an IMC. Finally, we propose an algorithm for counter-example generation, in case a refinement of two CMCs does not hold. We present a tool that implements our results. Implementing CMCs is a complex process and relies on recent advances made in decision procedures for theory of reals.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Delahaye, Benoit","Larsen, Kim Guldstrand","Legay, Axel","Pedersen, Mikkel Larsen","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-008439"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","INRIA/IRISA Rennes"],"keyword":["Abstraction","Compositional reasoning","Markov Chains","Reasoning about fault tolerance","Specification"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"new results for constraint markov chains","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.peva.2011.11.003","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-008439","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000308059000006","type":"wos"},{"id":"84864278194","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-af0b5bf7-0b87-4b8c-9fce-a337647bdf9c","itu-3fd534ef-4b8c-408f-9cf3-cebe2cbe0d50"],"keyword":["Abstraction","Compositional reasoning","Markov Chains","Reasoning about fault tolerance","Specification"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-28210E17261BA7E299E408B8C28C4874"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.peva.2011.11.003","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fr","key":"inria irisa rennes","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"INRIA/IRISA Rennes","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, CISS - Center for Embedded Software Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Distributed Systems and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Univers