{"abstract":"Notions of specification, implementation, satisfaction, and refinement, together with operators supporting stepwise design, constitute a specification theory. We construct such a theory for Markov Chains (MCs) employing a new abstraction of a Constraint MC. Constraint MCs permit rich constraints on probability distributions and thus generalize prior abstractions such as Interval MCs. Linear (polynomial) constraints suffice for closure under conjunction (respectively parallel composition). This is the first specification theory for MCs with such closure properties. We discuss its relation to simpler operators for known languages such as probabilistic process algebra. Despite the generality, all operators and relations are computable.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Caillaud, B.","Delahaye, B.","Larsen, Kim Guldstrand","Legay, Axel","Pedersen, Mikkel Larsen","Wa̧sowski, A."],"cuid":["S02-095.60-003195"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["France"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","INRIA/IRISA"],"keyword":["Abstraction","Compositional reasoning","Markov Chains","Process algebra","Specification theory"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"constraint markov chains","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tcs.2011.05.010","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.60-003195","identifier":[{"id":"79960017505","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000293119400001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-412cc0c1-4c49-4613-b3e3-96a1e394a99f","itu-7abc60f1-f112-43b9-9e4b-5be4de9a6730"],"keyword":["Abstraction","Compositional reasoning","Markov Chains","Process algebra","Specification theory"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8440B7DD030FDCD01110EFD4BFDAD2B0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tcs.2011.05.010","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fr","key":"inria irisa","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"INRIA/IRISA","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (TECH)","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"B.","key":"caillaudpau","last":"Caillaud","name":"Caillaud, B.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"B.","key":"delahayepau","last":"Delahaye","locid":"7f958ccf-6f8b-425b-a1a3-ef41554a85b9","name":"Delahaye, B.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim Guldstrand","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"27dbc400-17ea-4672-9343-63093ad486c9","name":"Larsen, Kim Guldstrand","orcid":"0000-0002-5953-3384","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A.","key":"legaypau","last":"Legay","locid":"8755f01e-c7cb-443a-bac8-1cfd63ba931c","name":"Legay, Axel","name_org":"Legay, A.","rank":4,"rolecode