{"abstract":"We present Clafer, a meta-modeling language with first-class support for feature modeling. We designed Clafer as a concise notation for meta-models, feature models, mixtures of meta- and feature models (such as components with options), and models that couple feature models and meta-models via constraints (such as mapping feature configurations to component configurations or model templates). Clafer also allows arranging models into multiple specialization and extension layers via constraints and inheritance. We identify four key mechanisms allowing a meta-modeling language to express feature models concisely and show that Clafer meets its design objectives using a sample product line. We evaluated Clafer and how it lends itself to analysis on sample feature models, meta-models, and model templates of an E-Commerce platform.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Bąk, Kacper","Czarnecki, Krzysztof","Wasowski, Andrzej"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382315"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Waterloo"],"keyword":["Constraint based modeling","Feature Modeling","Meta Modeling Language","Model Templates","Software Product Line"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feature and meta models in clafer mixed specialized and coupled","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/79952263668","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382315","identifier":[{"id":"79952263668","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-465c16fb-28c6-4a02-b84b-5d8d7b62d2c9"],"keyword":["Constraint-Based Modeling","Feature Modeling","Meta-Modeling Language","Model Templates","Software Product Line"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-02F650DB7464A803B7A3992CC0559FCA"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ca","key":"university of waterloo","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Waterloo","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kacper","key":"bąkpau","last":"Bąk","name":"Bąk, Kacper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Krzysztof","key":"czarneckipau","last":"Czarnecki","name":"Czarnecki, Krzysztof","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrzej","key":"wasowskipau","last":"Wasowski","locid":"a39b94ff-e1b6-4b96-8404-486167a9123d","name":"Wasowski, Andrzej","orcid":"0000-0003-0532-2685","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["03029743","16113349"],"issn_org":["03029743"],"journal":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","pages":"102-122","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","volume":"6563"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79952263668"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-465c16fb-28c6-4a02-b84b-5d8d7b62d2c9"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Feature and Meta-Models in Clafer: Mixed, Specialized, and Coupled","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382315","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
